<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<appendix xml:id="ch-chapter-appendix" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Appendix</title>

<introduction>
  <p>
    This appendix collects reference material that supports the main text but is not meant to be
    read sequentially. The topics included here provide tools, reminders, and summaries that are
    useful throughout the course, especially when working through examples or practice problems
    in the main chapters.
  </p>

  <p>
    The first section contains tables of integrals and related reference formulas that may be helpful
    when performing computations. The second section reviews key ideas from linear algebra, including
    matrices, determinants, and related concepts that appear naturally in multivariable calculus.
    These materials are intended as a refresher rather than a full development.
  </p>

  <p>You may return to this appendix as needed while studying the main chapters.
  </p>
</introduction>

  <section xml:id="app-integration-reference">
    <title>Integration Reference</title>
    <p>
  This section provides tables of integrals and related reference formulas commonly used in multivariable calculus.
  These tables are included for quick consultation during computations and examples and are not intended to replace
  conceptual understanding or derivations.
</p>
    <p>[Placeholder: integration reference tables / techniques.]</p>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="app-matrix-tools">
    <title>Matrix Tools for Multivariable Calculus</title>
    <p>
  This section reviews selected topics from linear algebra that arise naturally in multivariable calculus,
  including matrices, determinants, and related ideas. The material is presented as a brief refresher to
  support recall and application, rather than a full development of the subject.
</p>
    <p>[Placeholder: Jacobian/Hessian, RREF, determinants, eigenvalues, etc.]</p>
  </section>

</appendix>